1) Architecture Map
Frontend
- Vite + React 18 app with Tailwind UI.
- VAPI Web SDK handles call lifecycle + transcript events.
- SSE client subscribes to backend for comparison table updates (EventSource).
- Local state only; no Hathora integration.

Backend
- FastAPI app exposing:
  - POST /vapi/webhook: handles VAPI tool-calls, routes to query_analytics/display_comparison_table.
  - GET /api/table/{call_id}: polling for latest table.
  - GET /api/table-stream/{call_id}: SSE stream for table updates.
  - GET /api/schema: SQLite schema inspection.
  - GET /health: service/DB health.
- SQL execution against local SQLite file engagement.db.
- In-memory table_store + sse_queues keyed by VAPI call_id.

Data Flow (high level)
- User speaks → VAPI transcribes → LLM decides clarification or queries → VAPI tool-calls webhook → backend executes SQL → results returned to LLM → LLM speaks + calls display_comparison_table → backend publishes SSE → frontend renders table.

APIs
- VAPI API used by setup_vapi.py to create assistant/tools.
- Backend provides webhook + table streaming endpoints.

Auth
- None. Backend allows all origins, no auth on endpoints.

State Management
- Frontend: React useState + hooks.
- Backend: in-memory dicts keyed by call_id; ephemeral and per-process.

Build/Deploy
- Frontend: Vite build (tsc + vite build). No deployment scripts.
- Backend: uvicorn run in server.py main. No containerization.
- E2E script uses ngrok to expose local webhook and updates .env files.

