3) Key Request Flow (end-to-end journey)
Use case: “Why did product engagement drop last week?”
1. User taps mic → frontend calls VAPI start with ASSISTANT_ID.
2. VAPI streams transcript events to browser; UI updates status to listening/thinking.
3. LLM decides to clarify or query; if querying, sends tool-calls to backend /vapi/webhook.
4. Backend validate_sql (SELECT-only, blocked keywords) → executes query on engagement.db.
5. Backend returns results as a text table string to VAPI.
6. LLM synthesizes response; then calls display_comparison_table tool.
7. Backend stores table under call_id and streams SSE to /api/table-stream/{call_id}.
8. Frontend EventSource receives table and renders ComparisonTable.

